    {
      "id": "cite_note-21",
      "text": "^ Hannah was recruited as a Traitor in Episode 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "cite_note-22",
      "text": "^ James A. was recruited as a Traitor in Episode 2."
    },
    {
      "id": "cite_note-23",
      "text": "^ Kenny was recruited as a Traitor in Episode 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "cite_note-Recruit-25",
      "text": "^ The Traitors were asked to choose two players to have the opportunity to plead their case and be recruited as a Traitor. Whoever was not selected by the Traitors would be murdered. Maya and Richard both chose Amol and James A."
    },
    {
      "id": "cite_note-Dagger-30",
      "text": "^ At the end of the mission, one player was awarded The Dagger, making their vote count twice at the next round table. The Dagger was granted to Kenny by James A. and Maya."
    },
    {
      "id": "cite_note-33",
      "text": "^ Episode 8 ended before Kenny's deciding double vote was revealed making it carry over into episode 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "cite_note-34",
      "text": "^ During the round table, James A. disclosed that he was a Traitor and was unanimously banished. His vote, if he cast one, was not shown."
    },
    {
      "id": "cite_note-Tied-35",
      "text": "^ The first round of voting resulted in a tie. Per the rules, a second vote was held where the players involved in the tie would not vote and the remaining players could only vote for those who tied."
    }
